-365,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-brief,evidence.body,,,g8-ev-postflight-context,Post-flight analysis has cleared Armstrong and Scott of blame. Walt Cunningham has criticized aspects of their performance; Tom Stafford has argued that undocking from Agena was the wrong decision. Gene Kranz has identified a failure on the ground: too few contingency procedures for the docked phase. Frank Borman and Wally Schirra have defended the crew.,
-366,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-brief,history-hidden,,,g8-ev-postflight-context,"Automatic only in the later post-flight scene. Attributed paraphrase of H5, a secondary account; not a transcript or an investigation document reproduced here. Sources: H5.",
-367,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.intent,,,g8-back-crew-criticism,Side with Cunningham and Stafford and blame the crew's handling of the emergency.,
-368,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,ui.label,,,app,Glen says,
-369,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.statement,Glen Kurtz — FLIGHT,,g8-back-crew-criticism,I agree with the criticism. Armstrong and Scott's handling of the emergency deserves the blame.,
-370,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.cost,,,g8-back-crew-criticism,"Armstrong and Scott lose trust in Glen, and division within the astronaut corps deepens.",
-371,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.attraction,,,g8-back-crew-criticism,Gain Cunningham and Stafford's support by backing their criticism.,
-372,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.uncertainty,,,g8-back-crew-criticism,The analysis has cleared the crew; your endorsement may prolong the argument rather than settle it.,
-373,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.subtitle,,,g8-own-ground-contingencies,Ground contingency procedures,
-374,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.intent,,,g8-own-ground-contingencies,Accept responsibility for the ground's lack of docked-flight contingency procedures.,
-375,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.statement,Glen Kurtz — FLIGHT,,g8-own-ground-contingencies,"The ground didn't have enough contingency procedures for the docked phase. That's our failure, and we'll correct it. I won't blame Armstrong and Scott for bringing the spacecraft home.",
-376,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.cost,,,g8-own-ground-contingencies,Glen publicly accepts responsibility for a failure in the ground organization.,
-377,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.attraction,,,g8-own-ground-contingencies,Back the crew and commission procedures for emergencies while docked.,
-378,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,option.uncertainty,,,g8-own-ground-contingencies,Cunningham and Stafford may keep their objections even after the ground begins corrective work.,
-379,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-decision,decision.hint,,,g8-accountability-decision,"Read the post-flight findings and both positions, then choose the statement Glen will make.",
-380,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-receipt,label,,,g8-accountability-receipt,Statement recorded,
-381,g8-postflight,g8-accountability-receipt,briefing,,crew-blame,g8-accountability-receipt,"“I agree with the criticism. Armstrong and Scott's handling of the emergency deserves the blame.”
